  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 330 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThe center of an upper ridge glides over our region Thursday \nevening, headed toward the Four Corners. Ridging shall overspread \nmuch of the western US and Great Plains through early next week, \nleading to hot and mostly dry conditions. Except for highs in the \n90s in/near the higher terrain and portions of the Lower Trans \nPecos, triple digit heat is expected across most of the region \nthrough the period. Readings up to 105 degrees are forecast over \nportions of the northern Permian Basin and areas along the Pecos \nRiver most afternoons. However, the hottest conditions are \nexpected along the Rio Grande, especially within the Big Bend, \nwhere highs may reach up to 115 degrees. Temperatures most nights\nare progged to cool to the mid to upper 70s. Given several days \nof very hot conditions, it's important to practice heat safety. \nTake breaks when needed, stay hydrated, and limit time outdoors \nduring the hottest parts of the day. In stark contrast to last \nweek, low (<20%) chances of isolated shower/storm activity remains\nconfined to areas in the vicinity of the higher terrain during \nthe Long Term period.",
